{"verdict":"changes_requested","issues":[{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":27,"description":"The `options` object passed to `contentstack.Stack(options)` has no `live_preview` key. Without this, the Contentstack SDK never initializes its live preview subsystem, so `Stack.livePreview` is undefined and the `onEntryChange` subscription in ContentstackContext.tsx (line 118) will never fire. Every acceptance criterion depends on this SDK-level configuration being present.","suggestedFix":"Add a `live_preview` key to the options object: `live_preview: { management_token: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN, enable: !!CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN, host: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST }`. Read CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN and CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST from process.env with appropriate validation/logging."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/interface/contentstack.ts","line":1,"description":"No `includeDraft` field exists on IContentstackGetEntry, IContentstackGetSingleEntry, IContentstackGetSingletonEntry, ICreateQueryConfig, or ICreateEntryConfig. The public-facing functions (getEntry, getSingleEntry, getSingletonEntry, findSingletonEntry) do not accept or propagate includeDraft to the factory. This means draft content can never be fetched — the preview site will only show published content, failing the core acceptance criterion that draft entries render on the preview site.","suggestedFix":"Add `includeDraft?: boolean` to ICommonContentstackConfig (or each relevant interface). In ContentstackFactory.setCommonConfig or createContentTypeQuery, when includeDraft is true, call `query.addParam('include_draft', 'true')`. Propagate the flag through getEntry, getSingleEntry, getSingletonEntry, and findSingletonEntry."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":115","description":"The `onEntryChange` subscription casts `data as Partial<IContentstackContent>` without any runtime validation or type narrowing. The callback parameter is typed as `unknown`, but the cast to `Partial<IContentstackContent>` is an unsafe type assertion that bypasses TypeScript strict compliance. The actual shape of Contentstack's live preview callback data is not verified to match IContentstackContent's structure.","suggestedFix":"Define an explicit interface for the Contentstack live preview callback payload (e.g., `IContentstackLivePreviewEvent`), type the callback parameter accordingly, and validate/sanitize the incoming data before merging it into state. At minimum, add an explanatory comment justifying the cast if the SDK's types are insufficient."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":81","description":"`process.env.CONTENTSTACK_LIVE_PREVIEW` and `process.env.CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_KEY` are read directly inside the component body. Per review criteria, no hardcoded strings for configuration values — environment variable names should use named constants. Additionally, reading process.env in a React component is a Next.js anti-pattern that can cause issues with client-side rendering.","suggestedFix":"Extract environment variable names to constants in src/config/constants.ts. For Next.js, these should be read at build time via next.config or passed as props from getStaticProps/getServerSideProps."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"test/unit/","line":0,"description":"No vitest unit tests were added for the live preview functionality. The test/unit/ directory does not exist. Per review criteria, new features must have corresponding vitest unit tests mirroring the src/ path. There are zero tests verifying that setContent updates the context value, that the initial state matches defaultContent, that onEntryChange triggers updateContent, or that includeDraft propagates correctly.","suggestedFix":"Create test/unit/context/ContentstackContext.spec.tsx testing: (1) initial state matches defaultContent, (2) updateContent merges partial updates, (3) onEntryChange subscription calls updateContent when livePreview.enabled is true, (4) onEntryChange is not subscribed when livePreview.enabled is false. Also create test/unit/services/contentstack.spec.ts testing includeDraft propagation."},{"severity":"major","file":"src/components/contentstack/ContentstackLink/ContentstackLink.tsx","line":29","description":"ContentstackLink now reads livePreview from context and appends `live_preview` query params to hrefs. This is scope beyond the prescribed minimal fix — the root cause analysis prescribes changes only to ContentstackProvider (useState + onEntryChange) and contentstack.ts (live_preview SDK config). Adding preview params to links is a separate concern that adds complexity without addressing the core live preview mechanism.","suggestedFix":"Remove the ContentstackLink changes unless they are explicitly required by a separate acceptance criterion. The prescribed minimal fix achieves live preview through context state updates, not URL parameter appending."},{"severity":"major","file":"src/interface/content/contentCard.ts","line":14","description":"`previewId`, `isPreview`, and `previewTimestamp` fields were added to IContentCard. These fields are not part of the prescribed minimal fix and appear to be unused by any component in the reviewed files. This is over-engineering beyond what the acceptance criteria require.","suggestedFix":"Remove these fields unless they are consumed by a component that needs them. The prescribed fix achieves live preview through the context provider's state management, not through per-entry preview metadata."},{"severity":"major","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":95","description":"The useEffect that syncs defaultContent into state on every defaultContent prop change (lines 95-101) is redundant with the useState initializer on line 80. If defaultContent changes, the useState initializer already handles the first render, and this effect causes unnecessary re-renders and potential content overwrites when live preview has already updated the state. This can clobber live preview updates if the parent re-renders with the same defaultContent reference.","suggestedFix":"Remove this useEffect. If defaultContent truly needs to be re-synced when it changes, use a ref to track the previous defaultContent and only update when the reference actually changes, but the prescribed fix does not require this."},{"severity":"minor","file":"src/context/ContentstackContext.tsx","line":68","description":"`useContentstackContext` throws a generic `Error` when context is null. Per review criteria, proper EpamError subclasses (or project-equivalent error subclasses) should be used rather than generic Error throws.","suggestedFix":"Use a project-specific error class (e.g., ConfigError or a ContextError) instead of generic Error."}],"summary":"The implementation partially addresses the prescribed root cause — ContentstackProvider correctly switches from useMemo to useState and adds an updateContent callback. However, the change is blocked by three critical gaps: (1) the Contentstack SDK options object in src/services/contentstack.ts has no `live_preview` configuration, so Stack.livePreview will be undefined and the onEntryChange subscription will never fire; (2) no includeDraft flag is propagated through the service layer interfaces or functions, so draft content can never be fetched even if the preview callback worked; (3) zero unit tests exist for any of the new functionality. Additionally, the changes to ContentstackLink.tsx and contentCard.ts add scope beyond the prescribed minimal fix without addressing the core live preview mechanism. The implementation cannot meet any of the six verification criteria in its current state."}
{"verdict":"changes_requested","issues":[{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":48,"description":"The `options` object passed to `contentstack.Stack(options)` does NOT include a `live_preview` configuration block. The prescribed root-cause fix requires adding `live_preview: { enable: true, host: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST, preview_token: CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN }` to the options. Without this, the Contentstack SDK never processes live preview data — every downstream component is starved of preview content. This is the root cause identified in the RCA and it remains completely unaddressed.","suggestedFix":"Add `live_preview: { enable: true, host: process.env.CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_HOST, preview_token: process.env.CONTENTSTACK_PREVIEW_TOKEN }` to the `options` object (around line 48-68), following the existing env-var pattern used for `CONTENTSTACK_API_HOST`. Also add the corresponding env var destructuring at the top of the file."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/context/contentstackContext.tsx","line":22,"description":"The file exports a bare `createContext<IContentstackContext>({})` with NO Provider component, NO `useState`, NO `useEffect`, and NO `onEntryChange`/`onLiveUpdate` subscription. The prescribed client-side fix requires a `ContentstackProvider` component that initializes the Live Preview SDK and subscribes to `onEntryChange` events, merging incoming preview data into context state via `setContent`. Without a reactive Provider, the `useContent` hook (consumed by 236+ components) always returns the static SSR-provided default content. No real-time preview updates can ever reach any consumer. All acceptance criteria related to real-time/draft content display are unmet.","suggestedFix":"Create a `ContentstackProvider` component that: (1) replaces the static context with `useState` for `content`; (2) adds a `useEffect` that calls `LivePreview.init()` and subscribes to `onEntryChange` (or `onMessage`); (3) merges incoming preview entry data into existing content state via `setContent`; (4) wraps children with `<ContentstackContext.Provider value={...}>`. Import `@contentstack/live-preview-utils`."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"package.json","line":0,"description":"The `@contentstack/live-preview-utils` dependency is not installed anywhere in the project. No import of this package exists in the codebase. Without this SDK, no client-side WebSocket-based Live Preview subscription can be established, making real-time content updates impossible.","suggestedFix":"Add `@contentstack/live-preview-utils` to package.json dependencies and install it. Import it in the ContentstackProvider component."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/interface/contentstack.ts","line":4,"description":"`ICommonContentstackConfig`, `ICreateQueryConfig`, and `ICreateEntryConfig` interfaces were not updated with an optional `live_preview` parameter. The prescribed fix requires adding an optional `live_preview` field so that live preview hash data can flow through to Contentstack queries. Without it, queries will always return published content even if the Stack is configured for live preview.","suggestedFix":"Add `live_preview?: { hash?: string; url?: string }` (or equivalent) to `ICommonContentstackConfig` or to both `ICreateQueryConfig` and `ICreateEntryConfig`."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/services/contentstack.ts","line":120,"description":"`createContentTypeQuery` and `createContentTypeEntryQuery` do not call `query.includeFallback()` or pass `live_preview` context to the Contentstack query chain. Even if the Stack were initialized with live_preview config, queries will always return published content because the live_preview hash from URL params is never forwarded to the query.","suggestedFix":"In `setCommonConfig` or in `createContentTypeQuery`/`createContentTypeEntryQuery`, check for a `live_preview` config field and if present, call `query.includeFallback()` and pass the live_preview hash to the query chain."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/hooks/useContent.ts","line":5,"description":"`useContent` calls `useContext(ContentstackContext)` but there is no reactive Provider component supplying a changing value. The hook will always return the static value passed at render time. Even if Contentstack live preview events fired, there is no state setter to trigger re-renders of the 236+ consumers. The hook cannot propagate live preview updates as-is.","suggestedFix":"This is fixed implicitly by creating the `ContentstackProvider` with `useState` (see blocker on contentstackContext.tsx). Once the Provider supplies a reactive value, `useContent` will work without changes — but only if the Provider is actually implemented."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"src/pages/api/preview.ts","line":0,"description":"No `pages/api/preview.ts` route exists to enable Next.js draft mode. Without this, `getStaticProps` will not re-run on CMS edits and the live preview session cannot be established server-side. No `context.preview` or `context.previewData` is forwarded to Contentstack service calls in any page component.","suggestedFix":"Create `src/pages/api/preview.ts` that calls `setPreviewData` with the live_preview hash/token. Update `getStaticProps` in page components (e.g., `src/pages/[[...slug]].tsx`) to forward `context.preview`/`context.previewData` to `getSingleEntry`/`getEntry`/`findSingletonEntry` calls."},{"severity":"blocker","file":"test/unit/","line":0,"description":"No vitest unit tests exist for the Live Preview feature. There is no `test/unit/` directory at all. No tests mirror `src/context/` for a ContentstackProvider, no tests for `live_preview` config in Stack options, no tests for `includeFallback()` behavior, and no tests verifying reactive content updates via `onEntryChange`. The test count has not increased to cover this new feature, violating the requirement that new features have corresponding vitest unit tests.","suggestedFix":"Create vitest test files mirroring the src/ paths: `test/unit/services/contentstack.spec.ts` (verify live_preview in options), `test/unit/context/contentstackContext.spec.tsx` (verify Provider subscribes to onEntryChange and updates state), and `test/unit/hooks/useContent.spec.ts` (verify hook returns updated content when Provider state changes)."}],"summary":"The Live Preview feature (AMSD-2041) is completely unimplemented. None of the prescribed minimal fixes from the Root Cause Analysis were applied. (1) The Contentstack Stack `options` object has no `live_preview` config block — the SDK will never process preview data. (2) The `ContentstackContext` is a bare `createContext` with no Provider component, no `useState`, no `useEffect`, and no `onEntryChange` subscription — the 236+ consumers of `useContent` will always receive static SSR content. (3) The `@contentstack/live-preview-utils` SDK is not installed. (4) No `live_preview` fields were added to query/entry config interfaces. (5) No `includeFallback()` calls exist in the query chain. (6) No `pages/api/preview.ts` route exists for Next.js draft mode. (7) No `context.preview`/`previewData` forwarding in page components. (8) Zero unit tests for the feature. Every single acceptance criterion is unmet: draft content cannot be displayed (AC1), real-time updates are impossible (AC4, AC5), platform-specific preview cannot work (AC3), and even basic published content flow through a reactive provider is absent. This is a non-implementation, not an incomplete or over-engineered one."}
